{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_10ec3ced1b0716cebbcbd2a2c3d7862b2d8fcb258afb359b76c7612a6414e80e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"cactus-compute/needle@956840ff176b snapshot 60917bc650675824","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6adcca52300f405fdca7e2b086119d1af9136377331fbcbd9280e83a85cd1540","slc_abdd01234c4fcf6619c8018957ef23c177273e8c48c9899590c69b9c23717b2e"],"source_ids":["src_6559d3ef6e4d5fb5b8414d9e38d4fe96","src_76c380e9f3915540bfc83d876ba7e8f5"],"text":"The Python API exposes needle.Needle(tools, system, weights, tool_index_path, buffer_size), agent.run/complete/embed/reset, needle.tool, needle.Field, and needle.extract; tools can be decorated functions, Pydantic models, raw JSON schemas, or a JSON string.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1d420df65fb5faf82007fa72f2259b0162051296301856c51f473b188d73b4ee","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"cactus-compute/needle@956840ff176b snapshot 60917bc650675824","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_abca5874d924a9e74cbe18b4092da5b6e0e265d813fb53e7c1b8cf81ca19d99b"],"source_ids":["src_b88739974450536385313501a8bc2262"],"text":"The repository is the Python package cactus-needle covering inference, LoRA fine-tuning, and export; the inference engine is fetched once from Hugging Face and cached.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_270696d65805383ec97ef3c7814e31ec64b6b883df3b13e64def131e237f870e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"cactus-compute/needle@956840ff176b snapshot 60917bc650675824","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_210c9c5476b77edeb071303404ea42bbc168eb8dffbc78259260304204f56f15","slc_a8f4810d0ae7feb0f44dff0493f947c29f4cc19fe6aa96fca513db44575dabab"],"source_ids":["src_6559d3ef6e4d5fb5b8414d9e38d4fe96","src_b88739974450536385313501a8bc2262"],"text":"Every response carries a calibrated confidence score from a learned head, defined as the minimum of a post-hoc head score and the decoding probability of the call tokens; users set a threshold and escalate below it.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_348d2201733e5695078f30a40b91ddafa25cf0cd2b2e0e7d87ac019012ff9b96","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"cactus-compute/needle@956840ff176b snapshot 60917bc650675824","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_061fcd79aa13a53d20f6471ef6f4e2eb2bebb4e0d22e9575a2634b48a35c1582","slc_13b5fafd709523a20be3e7e1847a86f1b91622b78aa5f4c9dbdad7495d950b43","slc_24415a5d878c5c858a9a69125e056b9158a7d29fe1307dd5a160238bd7b1c681","slc_614158e154a81800e08a1964101192a4092a369d7418d6c6ddfde9ab35b277ee","slc_768e6c87b955793c8c9423401895616ce4abb9e3e91a2ea78a2b2c93baf4c5dd","slc_cc955ab81bdead23e5fd3f39e4fa8335c6edb1c51d43058f3ed24a4cb11908d7","slc_f97eb3b972379e184614508aa69fb26262c29d402e94b890f411206c7a0e833d"],"source_ids":["src_b88739974450536385313501a8bc2262"],"text":"The documented fine-tuning workflow is: optionally synthesize data via needle generate-data (needs OPENROUTER_API_KEY), LoRA fine-tune with needle finetune (defaults epochs 3, lora-rank 16, lr 1e-4), then merge and quantize with needle build into a .cact archive.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_527cef466feb87996281312d8fba7dd5282bf122bbcd45f59b202a367e63e0c3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"cactus-compute/needle@956840ff176b snapshot 60917bc650675824","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_e2a0158313aba9106d7a983fba89b2b90b2c7f744b73e9abc41984d8a4c80469"],"source_ids":["src_b88739974450536385313501a8bc2262"],"text":"The model is said to be compressed to CQ2-bit via Cactus Quants and built on the Simple Attention Network findings, baked into its own engine.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5ed679f2e3751906f4447a3da39fcd759fca00470c005f58ce48157e09f8fb21","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"cactus-compute/needle@956840ff176b snapshot 60917bc650675824","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_e2a0158313aba9106d7a983fba89b2b90b2c7f744b73e9abc41984d8a4c80469"],"source_ids":["src_b88739974450536385313501a8bc2262"],"text":"Needle 2 is described as an open 45M-parameter model for tool calling, device use and structured extraction, shipped as a single 14MB binary that runs a session in about 28MB of RAM.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6dc5efe24d6c7f87c67060a7435ab98d951335969ae7f7e09b193b4d8c77b5ee","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"cactus-compute/needle@956840ff176b snapshot 60917bc650675824","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_51c56e67ce798cf3b53b867d12603bc531a9a6d6b069559abdbcb53d80007a9f","slc_730632fbb3a6c5b235c103b43226e4e14990de9347bb91b4161f295d07947577","slc_9ac4aad13806c1af10f8e144cb9e35333240f7d20810d33f82ab8a5e549d7214","slc_ac568c93d69c4fa320a3182879fcd85ae01e48c99372cb649021de385a8ac253","slc_f4452e194dc93b031c0cc100527b7f8032febb7cc31787b34f477db3cfc3d94c"],"source_ids":["src_76c380e9f3915540bfc83d876ba7e8f5","src_b88739974450536385313501a8bc2262"],"text":"The runtime install excludes training; fine-tuning and export need the [train] extra (JAX, imported lazily), with [train,gpu] for CUDA and [train,metal] for Apple Silicon; Pydantic is used for typed extraction.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_91ac23d2434e7ee7770189d0be48da5f1878558cfb6ba0ee877e442f96305f56","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"cactus-compute/needle@956840ff176b snapshot 60917bc650675824","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_47c24118572fe5d7703f67968c7d27df6cf7152ea66e8a13ebe371699c829689","slc_abdd01234c4fcf6619c8018957ef23c177273e8c48c9899590c69b9c23717b2e"],"source_ids":["src_6559d3ef6e4d5fb5b8414d9e38d4fe96"],"text":"agent.run() drives a full agentic loop (max_steps=8 default): the model picks calls, Needle executes the user's Python functions, feeds results back, and returns final results; ungrounded fields are refused unless strict=False.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b073d68618295e2f8c1f250d99780f2a392de26d6043f2bd702bafa0c830bf56","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"cactus-compute/needle@956840ff176b snapshot 60917bc650675824","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_732c35294f0b0c85cb8e6ca23ae8cb522daeef5104e0da2273cf6916317bd7a3","slc_c44e0cf4e6b611bc5d39159fb1b454d62e202bd84c70e5cde3de70b1d708da14"],"source_ids":["src_6559d3ef6e4d5fb5b8414d9e38d4fe96","src_76c380e9f3915540bfc83d876ba7e8f5"],"text":"Each turn returns one JSON object with fields including type, success, error, function_calls, reasoning, confidence, prefill_tps, decode_tps, and peak_ram_mb; empty function_calls is the off-topic refusal.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d8073d6887fd543270ac5fc17e391f6154679e4a3bb9390a7be34bc512635444","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"cactus-compute/needle@956840ff176b snapshot 60917bc650675824","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_47c24118572fe5d7703f67968c7d27df6cf7152ea66e8a13ebe371699c829689","slc_a8f4810d0ae7feb0f44dff0493f947c29f4cc19fe6aa96fca513db44575dabab"],"source_ids":["src_6559d3ef6e4d5fb5b8414d9e38d4fe96","src_b88739974450536385313501a8bc2262"],"text":"Tool calls are constrained by a byte-level grammar compiled from the declared schemas, so output is structured JSON and cannot be malformed; the reasoning field is generated unconstrained.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_df2769309b4444b276236564b419700a85cde2a56aa5b21b4954b96582998b69","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"cactus-compute/needle@956840ff176b snapshot 60917bc650675824","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a8f4810d0ae7feb0f44dff0493f947c29f4cc19fe6aa96fca513db44575dabab"],"source_ids":["src_b88739974450536385313501a8bc2262"],"text":"The runtime uses a 256-token sliding window with tools pinned as KV sinks, which the README says keeps total memory near 28MB regardless of conversation length.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f170c7f8620d525fa3b69b90323ac4653aa4e10ee719e0d73995ee1b1e7814fe","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"cactus-compute/needle@956840ff176b snapshot 60917bc650675824","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_604f67c766af41949871b9cefd3c641d40963a0b4b2a6e4415bb13f6f7e35a27","slc_a8f4810d0ae7feb0f44dff0493f947c29f4cc19fe6aa96fca513db44575dabab"],"source_ids":["src_6559d3ef6e4d5fb5b8414d9e38d4fe96","src_b88739974450536385313501a8bc2262"],"text":"For catalogues above five tools, a built-in contrastive retrieval head embeds schemas at init and renders only the top five tools per turn, rebuilding the grammar over that subset.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:40:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ed8b945d28aa4763ae4aa9f74db5227c"}
